#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.area_summary:3 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Classifies each grid point (order, cutoff) as chaotic "
"(:math:`\\lambda_{\\max} > 0`, finite), periodic (:math:`\\lambda_{\\max}"
" \\le 0`, finite), or divergent (NaN or Inf). Returns absolute counts and"
" two complementary percentages: one over the full grid, another excluding"
" divergent points so the chaotic proportion is not artificially deflated "
"by parameter regions where the FIR filter itself becomes ill-conditioned."
msgstr ""
"Classifies each grid point (order, cutoff) as chaotic "
"(:math:`\\lambda_{\\max} > 0`, finite), periodic (:math:`\\lambda_{\\max}"
" \\le 0`, finite), or divergent (NaN or Inf). Returns absolute counts and"
" two complementary percentages: one over the full grid, another excluding"
" divergent points so the chaotic proportion is not artificially deflated "
"by parameter regions where the FIR filter itself becomes ill-conditioned."

#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.area_summary:12 of
msgid "A loaded sweep."
msgstr "A loaded sweep."

