msgstr "Return types"

#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.area_summary:15 of
msgid "Counts and percentages for the three dynamical regimes."
msgstr "Counts and percentages for the three dynamical regimes."

#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.lmax_statistics:3 of
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Filters the sweep grid by dynamical regime then computes mean, median, "
"standard deviation, min, max, and a bootstrap 95% confidence interval for"
" the mean."
msgstr ""
"Filters the sweep grid by dynamical regime then computes mean, median, "
"standard deviation, min, max, and a bootstrap 95% confidence interval for"
" the mean."

#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.lmax_statistics:9 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Subset of grid points to include: * ``\"chaotic\"`` — only points with "
":math:`\\lambda_{\\max} > 0` (finite) * ``\"all_finite\"`` — all finite "
"points (excludes NaN/Inf) * ``\"periodic\"`` — only points with "
":math:`\\lambda_{\\max} \\le 0` (finite)"
msgstr ""
"Subset of grid points to include: * ``\"chaotic\"`` — only points with "
":math:`\\lambda_{\\max} > 0` (finite) * ``\"all_finite\"`` — all finite "
"points (excludes NaN/Inf) * ``\"periodic\"`` — only points with "
":math:`\\lambda_{\\max} \\le 0` (finite)"

#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.lmax_statistics:14 of
msgid "Number of bootstrap resamples (default 1000)."
msgstr "Number of bootstrap resamples (default 1000)."

#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.lmax_statistics:16 of
msgid "RNG seed for reproducibility (default 42)."
msgstr "RNG seed for reproducibility (default 42)."

#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.lmax_statistics:19 of
msgid ""
"Descriptive statistics including bootstrap 95% CI. When fewer than 3 "
"valid points exist, the CI fields are NaN."
msgstr ""
"Descriptive statistics including bootstrap 95% CI. When fewer than 3 "
"valid points exist, the CI fields are NaN."

#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.load_all_sweeps:3 of
msgid ""
"Returns a dict keyed by ``(filter_type, window)`` for non-Kaiser sweeps "
"or ``(filter_type, \"kaiser_<beta>\")`` for Kaiser  beta-sweeps. Results "
"are cached in memory so repeated calls are free."
msgstr ""
"Returns a dict keyed by ``(filter_type, window)`` for non-Kaiser sweeps "
"or ``(filter_type, \"kaiser_<beta>\")`` for Kaiser  beta-sweeps. Results "
"are cached in memory so repeated calls are free."

#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.load_all_sweeps:7 of
msgid ""
"Root directory containing per-configuration subdirectories and an "
"optional ``kaiser/<filter_type>/beta_<N>`` subtree."
msgstr ""
"Root directory containing per-configuration subdirectories and an "
"optional ``kaiser/<filter_type>/beta_<N>`` subtree."

#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.load_all_sweeps:10 of
msgid "Mapping from ``(filter_type, window_key)`` to :class:`SweepResult`."
msgstr "Mapping from ``(filter_type, window_key)`` to :class:`SweepResult`."

#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.rank_configurations:3 of
msgid ""
"Mapping from ``(filter_type, window_key)`` to a loaded sweep. Typically "
"obtained via :func:`load_all_sweeps`."
msgstr ""
"Mapping from ``(filter_type, window_key)`` to a loaded sweep. Typically "
"obtained via :func:`load_all_sweeps`."

#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.rank_configurations:5 of
msgid "RNG seed forwarded to :func:`lmax_statistics` (default 42)."
msgstr "RNG seed forwarded to :func:`lmax_statistics` (default 42)."

#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.rank_configurations:7 of
msgid "Descending by ``n_chaotic``. Rank is 1-indexed."
msgstr "Descending by ``n_chaotic``. Rank is 1-indexed."

#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.top_k_per_filter:3 of
msgid ""
"Calls :func:`rank_configurations` internally, then groups the global "
"ranking by ``filter_type``, keeping at most *k* entries per group."
msgstr ""
"Calls :func:`rank_configurations` internally, then groups the global "
"ranking by ``filter_type``, keeping at most *k* entries per group."

#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.sweet_spot_per_filter:12
#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.top_k_per_filter:7 of
msgid "Mapping from ``(filter_type, window_key)`` to loaded sweeps."
msgstr "Mapping from ``(filter_type, window_key)`` to loaded sweeps."

#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.top_k_per_filter:8 of
msgid "Maximum number of entries per filter type (default 3)."
msgstr "Maximum number of entries per filter type (default 3)."

#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.top_k_per_filter:9 of
msgid "Forwarded to :func:`rank_configurations`."
msgstr "Forwarded to :func:`rank_configurations`."

#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.top_k_per_filter:11 of
msgid ""
"Keys are filter types; values are lists of at most *k* "
":class:`ConfigRank` entries, ordered by descending ``n_chaotic``."
msgstr ""
"Keys are filter types; values are lists of at most *k* "
":class:`ConfigRank` entries, ordered by descending ``n_chaotic``."

#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.consolidate_kaiser:3 of
msgid ""
"Non-Kaiser windows are passed through unchanged. This produces a balanced"
" dataset where each window family appears once per filter type, making "
"window-to-window comparisons fair."
msgstr ""
"Non-Kaiser windows are passed through unchanged. This produces a balanced"
" dataset where each window family appears once per filter type, making "
"window-to-window comparisons fair."

#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.consolidate_kaiser:7
#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.kaiser_beta_optimal:3 of
msgid "Mapping from :func:`load_all_sweeps`."
msgstr "Mapping from :func:`load_all_sweeps`."

#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.consolidate_kaiser:9 of
msgid ""
"Same shape as *sweep_results*, but with at most one Kaiser entry per "
"``filter_type`` (the β with the most chaotic points)."
msgstr ""
"Same shape as *sweep_results*, but with at most one Kaiser entry per "
"``filter_type`` (the β with the most chaotic points)."

#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.kaiser_beta_optimal:4 of
msgid "Forwarded to :func:`lmax_statistics`."
msgstr "Forwarded to :func:`lmax_statistics`."

#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.sweet_spot_per_filter:3 of
msgid ""
"For each filter type, scans all available window sweeps and returns the "
"exact ``(N_z, omega_c, window)`` where ``lambda_max`` is globally "
"maximal."
msgstr ""
"For each filter type, scans all available window sweeps and returns the "
"exact ``(N_z, omega_c, window)`` where ``lambda_max`` is globally "
"maximal."

#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.sweet_spot_per_filter:7 of
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The 95% confidence interval is computed from the per-point standard "
"deviation ``h_std`` and ``n_initial`` metadata via the t-distribution. If"
" ``h_std`` is NaN or ``n_initial`` is unavailable, the CI fields are "
"``None``."
msgstr ""
"The 95% confidence interval is computed from the per-point standard "
"deviation ``h_std`` and ``n_initial`` metadata via the t-distribution. If"
" ``h_std`` is NaN or ``n_initial`` is unavailable, the CI fields are "
"``None``."

#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.sweet_spot_per_filter:14 of
msgid "One entry per filter type that has at least one finite point."
msgstr "One entry per filter type that has at least one finite point."

#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.best_chaos_preserving:3 of
msgid "Returns the *top_n* entries with the most chaotic coverage."
msgstr "Returns the *top_n* entries with the most chaotic coverage."

#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.compare_filter_types:3 of
msgid ""
"Returns a ``dict`` keyed by filter type (``\"lowpass\"``, ...) with each "
"value being a :class:`FilterTypeAggregate` containing mean percentages "
"and lambda_max across all windows that use that filter type."
msgstr ""
"Returns a ``dict`` keyed by filter type (``\"lowpass\"``, ...) with each "
"value being a :class:`FilterTypeAggregate` containing mean percentages "
"and lambda_max across all windows that use that filter type."

#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.optimal_parameters:3 of
msgid "Filters results by *window* and *filter_type* if given."
msgstr "Filters results by *window* and *filter_type* if given."

#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.beta_summary:3 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Returns a nested dict: ``{filter_type: {beta: {pct_chaotic, mean_lmax, "
"...}}}``"
msgstr ""
"Returns a nested dict: ``{filter_type: {beta: {pct_chaotic, mean_lmax, "
"...}}}``"

#: chaotic_pfc.analysis.stats.beta_curve:3 of
msgid ""
"Useful for plotting the β-dependence of chaotic coverage. Returns empty "
"arrays when *filter_type* is absent from the data."
msgstr ""
"Useful for plotting the β-dependence of chaotic coverage. Returns empty "
"arrays when *filter_type* is absent from the data."

